# ============================================================
# PART 14 — BUILD THE CANDIDATE CLINICAL-EQUIPOISE COHORT
# ============================================================

Construct several nested populations.

### E0 — All post-TACE reassessments

### E1 — Active residual/recurrent HCC
Exclude clear complete/nonviable response.

### E2 — Liver-confined active disease
Exclude:
- definite extrahepatic progression
- definite major vascular invasion

### E3 — Clinically plausible repeat-TACE/systemic candidates
E2 plus no clearly catastrophic hepatic decompensation.

Do NOT require Child-Pugh because it is not reliably available.

Use objective structured hepatic reserve instead:
- ALBI
- bilirubin
- INR
- creatinine
- sodium
- ascites
- encephalopathy

### E4 — Treatment-decision cohort
E3 restricted to patients who actually receive within 90 days:

- repeat TACE
OR
- systemic therapy

For each population report branch counts.

